.nh
.TH "PB-ACCESS-TUNNEL" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-access-tunnel - Open private TCP access to a private tunnel route


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb access tunnel <tunnel-or-route> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Open private TCP access to an existing private tunnel route, selected by tunnel or route ID.
The command opens a loopback listener on this computer, prints its address and keeps the access
alive with periodic heartbeats; the access is released when the command ends or stops
heartbeating.

.PP
--listen must be a literal loopback address, 127.0.0.1 or ::1 with an optional port; the
default 127.0.0.1:0 picks a free port.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for tunnel

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical JSON

.PP
\fB--listen\fP="127.0.0.1:0"
	loopback address to listen on, 127.0.0.1 or ::1 with optional port (default: a free port)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb access tunnel myroute
  pb access tunnel tun_abc123 --listen 127.0.0.1:8080
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-access(1)\fP
